 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib defines `kronecker := kroneckerMap (\u00b7 * \u00b7)` and `kroneckerMap f A B := of fun i j => f (A i.1 j.1) (B i.2 j.2)` (Kronecker.lean:55,274). Grepping Mathlib and TauCeti for `matrix_kronecker` or Kronecker continuity finds nothing; the analogous `Continuous.matrix_vecMulVec` is at Topology/Instances/Matrix.lean:171.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Probability/Distributions/MatrixNormal/Continuity.lean",
   "fix": "Add `Continuous.matrix_kronecker` (continuous `A`, `B` give continuous `fun x \u21a6 A x \u2297\u2096 B x`), proved via `continuous_matrix` and `Matrix.kroneckerMap_apply`. Then derive `hcov` from it or with `fun_prop`.",
   "issue": "`hcov` proves continuity of `U ij.2 kl.2`-style products and closes the `(V \u2297\u2096 U) ij kl` goal by silently unfolding `kronecker`/`kroneckerMap`/`Matrix.of`. It also inlines a reusable fact (continuity of the Kronecker product) that exists neither in Mathlib nor in TauCeti.",
   "line": 52
  },
  {
   "evidence": "`def vec (A : Matrix m n R) : n \u00d7 m \u2192 R := fun ij => A ij.2 ij.1` (Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Vec.lean:40).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Probability/Distributions/MatrixNormal/Continuity.lean",
   "fix": "Make the unfolding explicit (`simp only [Matrix.vec]`, or a small `Continuous.matrix_vec` lemma), or add a comment saying the step is definitional.",
   "issue": "`continuous_pi fun ij \u21a6 continuous_fst.matrix_elem ij.2 ij.1` closes `Continuous fun p \u21a6 p.1.vec ij` only by silently unfolding `Matrix.vec`, and no comment says so.",
   "line": 46
  }
 ],
